014 can be used in Outside Hand, or pung for 2 points.\n\nB7: middle \u2014 cannot be used in Outside Hand.\n\nT6: middle \u2014 same.\n\nSo **B1 is more valuable than T6 or B7**\n\nThus, **discard T6 or B7**\n\nBetween them, **T6** is not part of a pair, **B7 is**.\n\nSo **B7 has more potential** \u2014 keep the pair.\n\nTherefore, **discard T6**\n\nIt\u2019s the only tile with no investment and no pattern value.\n\nEvaluation: The goal is to aim for high-scoring patterns like All Pungs (6 points) and Outside Hand (4 points). Discarding T6 removes a middle-suited tile that hinders Outside Hand and has no meld value. Keeping the pair of B7 offers slight flexibility for a future pung, while winds and dragons are valuable for scoring. T6 is the least useful tile in hand.\n\nReason: T6 is a middle-suited tile not contributing to any major pattern, not part of a pair, and its discard supports the pursuit of Outside Hand by removing an ineligible tile.\n\nAnswer: Play T6"}
